    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d740">

                <pb facs="0838" n="828" xml:id="pg828"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.AD1/25: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vincent</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-31T09:00:00+07:00">March 31, 1943—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>475. Minister of Foreign Affairs<anchor n="16" xml:id="d740-f1"/> has informed me
                    that Chinese Government has no objection to the inclusion of the four named in
                    Department’s 399, March 24, 10 p.m.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office has asked me to obtain from Department some indication of the size
                    of the delegation expected. I have stated that as many delegates as might be
                    reasonably expected effectively to serve would be welcome; that in view of
                    transportation difficulties it might be advisable to limit delegation to less
                    than 10 persons; but that I would try to obtain an opinion from Department on
                    the question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vincent</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
